<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111375" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλό-πατρις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, but acc.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόπατριν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.14.4
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.235
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Diod.Tars.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cleom.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Peregr.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, etc.:—<i>loving one's country, patriotic,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
			</span></i> l.c., <u>AP</u> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				9.10.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fab.</u>
				12
			</span></i>, etc.; freq. as honorary title, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				804.12
			</span></i> (Cos, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοπάτριδας</span> (acc. pl.) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ φιλοπάτορας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Sardis</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>).No.<i><span class="en">
				41
			</span></i>*.<i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φιλόπατρι,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοπατρία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.119c
			</span></i>.</div>
